   2018},
Abstract = {This study was aimed to examine the interplay of academic efficacy, goal
   orientation toward academic achievement. 199 first and second year
   university students in Indonesia were selected as respondents. The
   Pattern of Adaptive Learning Scales (PALS) was used to measure the
   academic efficacy and goal orientation. The finding revealed that
   mastery goal orientation is a considerable factor for academic
   achievement. This finding can be used in the context of improving
   educational quality achievement in Indonesia.},
