   musical training based on pitch processing could help eight-year-old
   children detect pitch changes in language. Results show that a
   relatively short exposure (eight weeks) to pitch processing in music
   exerts some influence on pitch processing in language. Therefore, these
   results are in line with the hypothesis that common processes may
   underlie pitch processing in language and in music.},
