   Society-for-Industrial-and-Organizational-Psychology, SAN DIEGO, CA, APR
   27-29, 2001},
Organization = {Soc Ind \& Org Psychol},
Abstract = {Upward feedback from subordinates was provided to Australian managers in
   an international professional services firm. The job performance of the
   managers in this quasi-experimental study was observed by subordinates
   to be significantly higher six months later, compared to both initial
   performance and subordinate ratings of a comparison group. Self-efficacy
   moderated this finding, suggesting that it plays a key role in
   determining behavioral reactions to upward feedback. The managers'
   learning goal orientation correlated significantly with their subsequent
   performance.},
