   2001},
Organization = {Eastern Acad Management},
Abstract = {Most research on selection processes and organizational fit deals with
   existing, unfilled positions where expectations and tasks are known and
   measurable. This article instead evaluates the reasons, processes, and
   implications of opportunistic hiring-hiring employees before their jobs
   exist. Examples from an exploratory study show how `'fit{''} factors
   into selection decisions. A typology is offered along the dimensions of
   whether opportunistic hiring is used to meet immediate or anticipated
   needs and the extent to which these needs are articulated prior to
   selection. (c) 2005 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.},
